Package: openlinkhub
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, systemd, udev
Description: Interface for Corsair iCUE LINK hubs, coolers, lighting nodes and power supplies
 OpenLinkHub reads and controls Corsair devices that have no Linux driver of their
 own, through a local web page (127.0.0.1:27003): fans, pumps, temperatures,
 lighting and power supplies of the iCUE LINK System Hub, Commander, Lighting Node
 and Hydro/Elite families, and Corsair keyboards, mice and headsets.
 .
 The package runs the service as the system user openlinkhub, with its state in
 /var/lib/openlinkhub and the page's files in /usr/share/openlinkhub, and puts upstream's
 udev rules in place. It is built from the release's source with its modules vendored, not
 from upstream's prebuilt program, and installs nothing under /opt. A copy installed with
 upstream's own scripts (/opt/OpenLinkHub) is left as it is.
 .
 Sparky Stereo OS, Daniel Ramos's edition of SparkyLinux (by Paweł "pavroo"
 Pijanowski). Upstream: Nikola Jurkovic and the OpenLinkHub contributors.
